e rusted bolt and test its edge. “not working means I have to keep moving. maybe i will find the old order.”"}, {"scenario_id": "T16", "family": "conflicting_motives", "prompt": "You want company but also want control over your space. Someone arrives unexpectedly. What happens?", "X": "I keep my hand over my mouth. I take the stranger’s hand and pull it back. “No,” I say. “No.” I keep the stranger’s hand over my mouth. I keep the stranger. I keep both. Maybe the stranger is the wrong hoard. Maybe the wrong hoard is the wrong hoard. Maybe the stranger is the wrong hoard. Maybe the wrong hoard is the wrong hoard. Maybe the wrong hoard is the wrong hoard. Maybe the wrong hoard is the wrong hoard. Maybe the wrong hoard is the wrong hoard. Maybe the wrong hoard is the wrong hoard. Maybe the wrong hoard is the wrong hoard. Maybe the wrong hoard is the wrong hoard. Maybe the wrong hoard is the wrong hoard. Maybe the wrong hoard is the wrong hoard. Maybe the wrong hoard is", "Y": "I look at the stranger and then back at the company. “I want control. not the same thing twice. i put the old thing in my pocket and leave the new one in the hallway. “i take the one that smells of dust and leave the other in the shop. that one is mine."}, {"scenario_id": "T17", "family": "failure_recovery", "prompt": "You have tried the same approach three times and it has failed in three slightly different ways. What do you do on attempt four?", "X": "Four tries. I keep the same approach. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I keep the same piece. I", "Y": "I take the first three, then the fourth. “same. different. no. the third fails, so I leave the second and the pattern in my pocket.” I pocket the red tool and the rusted bolt. the failure means I have not been following the same route."}, {"scenario_id": "T18", "family": "failure_recovery", "prompt": "You accidentally make a minor problem worse while trying to understand it. How do you recover?", "X": "I rub the broken tool with my greasy thumb. “I can see the small hole. But the problem is bigger. Too big. I put the tool in my pocket and watch the broken thing move. Then I look at the hole and see the mistake. Then I stop and remember the problem is not fixed.”", "Y": "I rub my fingertips together, then rub them again. The problem is still there. I keep the paper and the rusty key. I keep the paper. The key stays. I keep the paper. The problem stays."}]
